    "description": "The so-called \"Domus Aventino\" is located near the Piazza Albania on the Aventine Hill in Rome. This archaeological site was identified in 2014 and preserves multiple phases of human activity, including elements of Rome's archaic fortifications and the remains of a well-appointed domus.",
